      ":question/id": "42ae0a26-1929-53f5-8f39-a8b4574fe62b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(75^\\circ\\right)$ without using a calculator?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $75^\\circ=30^\\circ+45^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(75^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ+45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)+\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
